/T (Hands-on experience: In my project, Jenkins agents ran on EC2 with an IAM role, so pushing to ECR needed no access keys. The database password lived in AWS Secrets Manager, and External Secrets Operator created the Kubernetes Secret in the namespace. When we rotated the password, the pod picked up the new value after a restart, with no change to the pipeline.)
/E (Hands-on experience: In my project, Jenkins agents ran on EC2 with an IAM role, so pushing to ECR needed no access keys. The database password lived in AWS Secrets Manager, and External Secrets Operator created the Kubernetes Secret in the namespace. When we rotated the password, the pod picked up the new value after a restart, with no change to the pipeline.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
