/T (Short answer: A Quality Gate is a set of pass/fail conditions in SonarQube. For example: no new critical bugs, test coverage on new code above 80%, and duplication below 3%. If the code does not meet these conditions, the gate fails, and we stop the pipeline so poor- quality code does not move forward.)
/E (Short answer: A Quality Gate is a set of pass/fail conditions in SonarQube. For example: no new critical bugs, test coverage on new code above 80%, and duplication below 3%. If the code does not meet these conditions, the gate fails, and we stop the pipeline so poor- quality code does not move forward.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
