/T (Short answer: agent any tells Jenkins to run the pipeline \(or stage\) on any available node that has a free executor. It is simple, but in production we usually use a specific label instead, because not every agent has the right tools like Docker or Maven.)
/E (Short answer: agent any tells Jenkins to run the pipeline \(or stage\) on any available node that has a free executor. It is simple, but in production we usually use a specific label instead, because not every agent has the right tools like Docker or Maven.)
