/T (Short answer: First I check the service status and the Jenkins logs to find why it stopped. The common causes are a Java version problem after an upgrade, a full disk, low memory, a port conflict, a broken plugin, or wrong permissions on JENKINS_HOME. I fix the cause, start the service, and confirm it is healthy.)
/E (Short answer: First I check the service status and the Jenkins logs to find why it stopped. The common causes are a Java version problem after an upgrade, a full disk, low memory, a port conflict, a broken plugin, or wrong permissions on JENKINS_HOME. I fix the cause, start the service, and confirm it is healthy.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
