/T (Hands-on experience: In my project, Jenkins suddenly became unreachable after a server restart. The service was running and curl localhost:8080 worked. The problem was the EC2 public IP had changed after the stop/start. We moved Jenkins behind an Application Load Balancer with a fixed DNS name and HTTPS, so it never happened again.)
/E (Hands-on experience: In my project, Jenkins suddenly became unreachable after a server restart. The service was running and curl localhost:8080 worked. The problem was the EC2 public IP had changed after the stop/start. We moved Jenkins behind an Application Load Balancer with a fixed DNS name and HTTPS, so it never happened again.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
