/T (Short answer: In Blue-Green deployment we run two identical environments. Blue is live; Green gets the new version. After testing Green, we switch the traffic from Blue to Green in one step. If something goes wrong, we switch back to Blue immediately, so rollback takes seconds and users see almost no downtime.)
/E (Short answer: In Blue-Green deployment we run two identical environments. Blue is live; Green gets the new version. After testing Green, we switch the traffic from Blue to Green in one step. If something goes wrong, we switch back to Blue immediately, so rollback takes seconds and users see almost no downtime.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [29]
>>
