/T (Hands-on experience: On EC2, I put JENKINS_HOME on a separate EBS volume and took daily EBS snapshots with AWS Backup. When we moved Jenkins to a bigger instance, I just detached the volume and attached it to the new instance. We also managed the system configuration as code with the Configuration as Code \(JCasC\) plugin, so a fresh Jenkins could be rebuilt from YAML.)
/E (Hands-on experience: On EC2, I put JENKINS_HOME on a separate EBS volume and took daily EBS snapshots with AWS Backup. When we moved Jenkins to a bigger instance, I just detached the volume and attached it to the new instance. We also managed the system configuration as code with the Configuration as Code \(JCasC\) plugin, so a fresh Jenkins could be rebuilt from YAML.)
