1986 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 402 0 R
/T (Short answer: Nodes let Jenkins spread builds across many machines. Without them, every build runs on the controller, which becomes slow and unsafe. With nodes, we can run many builds in parallel, use different operating systems and tools, keep the controller stable, and isolate sensitive work like production deployments.)
/E (Short answer: Nodes let Jenkins spread builds across many machines. Without them, every build runs on the controller, which becomes slow and unsafe. With nodes, we can run many builds in parallel, use different operating systems and tools, keep the controller stable, and isolate sensitive work like production deployments.)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
