/T (Hands-on experience: One agent kept going offline every afternoon. The node log said the disk space was below the threshold. Docker images and old workspaces were filling the disk. I cleaned it, added a nightly cleanup job \(docker system prune -af --filter "until=72h"\), and later moved those builds to Kubernetes pod agents, which start clean every time.)
/E (Hands-on experience: One agent kept going offline every afternoon. The node log said the disk space was below the threshold. Docker images and old workspaces were filling the disk. I cleaned it, added a nightly cleanup job \(docker system prune -af --filter "until=72h"\), and later moved those builds to Kubernetes pod agents, which start clean every time.)
/Pg 66 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
