/T (Short answer: In a Declarative Jenkinsfile, I add several stage blocks inside stages. They run one after another by default. I can control them with when conditions, run some in parallel, give each its own agent, and group related stages using nested stages. Then I create a Pipeline or Multibranch job that points to this Jenkinsfile.)
/E (Short answer: In a Declarative Jenkinsfile, I add several stage blocks inside stages. They run one after another by default. I can control them with when conditions, run some in parallel, give each its own agent, and group related stages using nested stages. Then I create a Pipeline or Multibranch job that points to this Jenkinsfile.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [3]
>>
