/T (Short answer: I would keep the logic generic and data-driven: one pipeline that reads a list of services, detects which ones changed, and builds and deploys only those, in parallel. The common steps come from a Shared Library. For the deploy, I would update each service's tag in the GitOps repo in one commit, and ArgoCD syncs all of them to Dev. Design points)
/E (Short answer: I would keep the logic generic and data-driven: one pipeline that reads a list of services, detects which ones changed, and builds and deploys only those, in parallel. The common steps come from a Shared Library. For the deploy, I would update each service's tag in the GitOps repo in one commit, and ArgoCD syncs all of them to Dev. Design points)
/Pg 72 0 R
/K [2]
