2542 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 419 0 R
/T (Short answer: There are two connections. First, Jenkins can use Kubernetes to run its agents through the Kubernetes plugin: each build gets a temporary pod. Second, Jenkins can deploy to Kubernetes, either directly with kubectl or Helm using a kubeconfig or service account credential, or indirectly through GitOps, where Jenkins updates Git and ArgoCD deploys.)
/E (Short answer: There are two connections. First, Jenkins can use Kubernetes to run its agents through the Kubernetes plugin: each build gets a temporary pod. Second, Jenkins can deploy to Kubernetes, either directly with kubectl or Helm using a kubeconfig or service account credential, or indirectly through GitOps, where Jenkins updates Git and ArgoCD deploys.)
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
