/T (Short answer: The usual reasons are: dependencies downloading every build because there's no local cache or Nexus proxy, slow tests running one by one, clean rebuilding everything, a large multi-module project built without parallel threads, low CPU or memory on the agent, snapshot update checks, and network slowness to the repository. I check the build log timestamps to find which part is slow, then fix that part.)
/E (Short answer: The usual reasons are: dependencies downloading every build because there's no local cache or Nexus proxy, slow tests running one by one, clean rebuilding everything, a large multi-module project built without parallel threads, low CPU or memory on the agent, snapshot update checks, and network slowness to the repository. I check the build log timestamps to find which part is slow, then fix that part.)
/Pg 85 0 R
/K [4]
>>
