2941 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 432 0 R
/T (Short answer: A concurrency issue happens when two pipeline runs work at the same time on something shared: the same environment, the same Git repo, the same workspace or the same image tag. For example, two deployments to Dev at once, or two)
/E (Short answer: A concurrency issue happens when two pipeline runs work at the same time on something shared: the same environment, the same Git repo, the same workspace or the same image tag. For example, two deployments to Dev at once, or two)
/Pg 90 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2942 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 432 0 R
/T (70. If the version 1.2 deployment fails but version 1.1 is stable, what will you do?)
/E (70. If the version 1.2 deployment fails but version 1.1 is stable, what will you do?)
/Pg 90 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2943 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 432 0 R
/T (Short answer: My first priority is to restore service, so I roll back to 1.1 immediately. Then I inform the team and stakeholders. After production is stable, I investigate 1.2 in a lower environment, find the root cause, fix it, and release a corrected version like 1.2.1 through the normal pipeline. Finally, we do a blameless post-mortem and add checks to catch this earlier.)
/E (Short answer: My first priority is to restore service, so I roll back to 1.1 immediately. Then I inform the team and stakeholders. After production is stable, I investigate 1.2 in a lower environment, find the root cause, fix it, and release a corrected version like 1.2.1 through the normal pipeline. Finally, we do a blameless post-mortem and add checks to catch this earlier.)
/Pg 90 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
