7146 0 obj
<<
/Title (Short answer: Our rollback depends on the deployment method. With GitOps, we revert the image tag commit and ArgoCD deploys the previous version. With Helm, we use helm rollback. With plain Kubernetes, kubectl rollout undo. We also have a parameterized "Rollback" job that redeploys any previous image tag, and we automate rollback when health checks fail after a deploy.)
/Dest [88 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7116 0 R
/Next 7172 0 R
>>
endobj
7147 0 obj
<<
/Title (Helm's --atomic flag \(called --rollback-on-failure in Helm 4\) can also roll back automatically if the upgrade fails.)
/Dest [89 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7116 0 R
/Prev 7173 0 R
>>
endobj
