/Title (Short answer: agent any tells Jenkins to run the pipeline \(or stage\) on any available node that has a free executor. It is simple, but in production we usually use a specific label instead, because not every agent has the right tools like Docker or Maven.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 8005 0 R
/Prev 8021 0 R
/Next 8008 0 R
>>
endobj
8013 0 obj
<<
/Title (The agent directive decides where the pipeline runs. Options:)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 8008 0 R
>>
endobj
8014 0 obj
<<
/Title (Short answer: A label is a tag we give to agents, like linux, docker, maven or windows. In the pipeline we ask for a label, and Jenkins runs the job only on agents with that label. It is how we send the right work to the right machine.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 8009 0 R
/Next 8022 0 R
>>
endobj
