/Title (How they talk: the controller sends build instructions to the agent through the remoting channel \(over SSH, TCP or WebSocket\), and the agent sends logs and results back. Hands-on experience: In my project, the controller ran on one EC2 instance with an EBS volume for JENKINS_HOME. All builds ran on agents. When an agent had issues, we just took it offline and replaced it, without any impact on Jenkins itself.)
