/Title (Short answer: An agent is a machine or container that runs the build work for the Jenkins controller. The controller sends the job to an agent, the agent runs the steps and streams the logs back. Agents connect over SSH \(controller connects to the agent\), as inbound agents \(agent connects to the controller\), or are created on demand by cloud plugins like EC2 or Kubernetes.)
/Dest [63 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 8122 0 R
/Next 8193 0 R
>>
